{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>Kindled.</b> The jealousy, or this [refers to] what they did, for we find this word used [in construct] as in כִּי אֵשׁ קָדַחְתָּ בְאַפִּי (Deuteronomy 32:22). And it is possible that קָדְחָה is like נִקְדְּחָה, like כָּל אֵלֶּה חָבְרוּ נֶחְבָּרוּ. All of this is a designation for the burning of anger." "<b>To the lowest Sheol.</b> Like the sense of גָּפְרִית וּמֶלַח שְׂרֵפָה כָּל אַרְצָהּ." "<b>And it shall devour earth.</b> Israel." "<b>And it shall flame.</b> From the root of לַהַט הַחֶרֶב." "<b>Mountains.</b> The mountains of Israel."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:26:07.528265283Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}